  "goodToKnow": "Die Anekdote is an anecdote: eine Anekdote erzählen. Anekdotisch means anecdotal: anekdotische Evidenz. In German literature, Johann Peter Hebel and Heinrich von Kleist wrote short, pointed Anekdoten and Kalendergeschichten (calendar stories), still read in schools. Anecdotes about Frederick the Great (der Alte Fritz) are a genre of their own. From Greek anekdotos (unpublished). Plural: die Anekdoten."
